Tailfin documentation — all rights reserved
===========================================

Copyright (C) 2026 Tailfinsim. All rights reserved.

This directory is NOT covered by the GNU Affero General Public License in
`/LICENSE`. That licence covers Tailfin's source code; this directory is
documentation and is licensed separately, which is to say: not licensed.

What this covers
----------------

Everything in `docs/`, including:

  - `tailfin-design-doc.md` — the design document and its appendices
  - `adr/` — the architecture decision records
  - every other document in this directory and its subdirectories

You may read it. GitHub's terms permit viewing and forking a public
repository, and nothing here objects to that. You may not otherwise copy,
adapt, republish or redistribute it, and no licence to do so is granted by
implication, by the presence of the AGPL on the code, or by this file.

Why the split
-------------

The code is copyleft because Tailfin is a hosted service and the AGPL is what
stops a closed hosted fork of it. That reasoning is about software.

The design document is a different kind of thing: it is the game's design,
worked out over a long time, and it is the part that would be most valuable to
someone building a competitor and least protected by a licence written for
programs. Keeping it reserved is a deliberate choice rather than an oversight,
and the practical effect is the intended one — a fork inherits the simulation,
not the appendices that explain why it behaves as it does.

Contributions
-------------

A contribution to `docs/` is offered under these terms rather than under the
AGPL. If that is not what you intend, say so in the pull request rather than
assuming; see `CONTRIBUTING.md`.

Third-party material
--------------------

Where a document quotes or reproduces third-party material, that material
remains under its own terms and this file does not extend to it. See
`/THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.md`.
